paper_summary:
**CUDRT establishes a comprehensive bilingual benchmark for assessing AI-generated text detection across various operations, addressing limitations in existing frameworks.**
- Introduces five operational categories for text generation: *Create*, *Update*, *Delete*, *Rewrite*, and *Translate* to encompass diverse LLM functionalities.
- Utilizes extensive datasets for each operational category, improving evaluation quality of existing text detectors in both *Chinese* and *English*.
- Employs a robust benchmark evaluation framework that supports scalable and reproducible experiments, ensuring a thorough assessment of AI text detectors' performance.
- Highlights the *limitations* of current benchmarks which predominantly focus on English and specific scenarios, suggesting a gap in capturing multilanguage nuances and diverse applications of LLMs.
- Experimental results provide insights for optimizing detector accuracy and suggest *future research* directions for improving detection methodologies.

Equation for text generation categorization:
$$
	ext{CUDRT}(text) = \begin{cases}
	ext{Create}, & 	ext{if task: completion/question answering} \\
	ext{Update}, & 	ext{if task: polish/expand} \\
	ext{Delete}, & 	ext{if task: summary/refine} \\
	ext{Rewrite}, & 	ext{if task: clarity/improvement} \\
	ext{Translate}, & 	ext{if task: English-Chinese translation}
	ext{Undefined}, & 	ext{if task: not categorized}
	ext{End cases}
	ext{CUDRT}
	ext{for }	ext{each }	ext{task}
	ext{assigned }	ext{as} \\in 	ext{CUDRT}
	ext{categoric description}.
	ext{End}
	ext{evaluation.}
	ext{Assign }	ext{score.}
	ext{return }	ext{result}
	ext{for }	ext{detection performance.}
	ext{End}
	ext{CUDRT}
$$
This equation categorizes text generation tasks essential for benchmarking AI-generated text detection.
